     <section anchor="introduction" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-2">
       <name slugifiedName="name-introduction">Introduction</name>
-      <t indent="0" pn="section-2-1">In cases where a manager must obtain performance history data about
-the behavior of equipment it manages several strategies can be
-followed in the design of a MIB that represents the managed
-equipment, including:
-0    The agent counts events on a continuous basis and,
-     whenever desired, the manager obtains the value of the event
-     counter and adjusts its understanding of the history of events
-     at the agent.</t>
-      <t indent="0" pn="section-2-2">0    The agent allocates events to 'buckets' where each bucket
-     represents an interval of time.</t>
